Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedjson.shoddy — reckoner seed: json.shoddy, converting at the
Rem bridge
Rem
Rem JSONPARSE, JSONTEXT, JSONPRETTY, JSONLOAD and JSONSAVE. Per R4.16
Rem there is no DOCUMENT cell at the keyboard: a Json value converts to
Rem and from the same shapes every other seed already uses — JNum,
Rem JStr and JBool onto the matching cell, JArr onto a LIST, and JObj
Rem onto a LIST of PAIRs, exactly the "dict" shape seeddict.shoddy
Rem already established. A parsed object is a dict the moment it lands
Rem on the stack: DGET, DHAS and DKEYS from seeddict work on it
Rem unchanged, and DPUT grows it.
Rem
Rem THE ONE GAP: JNull and an empty array both convert to the same
Rem empty LIST { }, and so both write back out as []. JSON's own type
Rem tells them apart; nothing on this stack does, and giving null a
Rem cell of its own is exactly the R4.16 growth this seed is built to
Rem avoid. A document that leans on the difference will not round-trip
Rem — everything else does.
Rem
Rem JSONLOAD and JSONSAVE go through TRYREADFILE/TRYWRITEFILE rather
Rem than json.shoddy's own JsonLoad/JsonSave, which are built on the
Rem aborting ReadFile/WriteFile (R3.5(a)). JSONPARSE reads through
Rem JsonRead, the total half of JsonParse, for the same reason: a
Rem bridged word must refuse, never abort, on bad input.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "json.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- Json <-> Cell, at the bridge ----------------------------------

Rem Total: every Cell shape has SOME Json answer, even one nothing here
Rem otherwise produces. A PAIR met on its own, a MATRIX, MONEY and a
Rem PROGRAM have no natural JSON shape, so each becomes the text it
Rem already renders as at the prompt — the same CutShow every stack
Rem word's own answer goes through.
Def JcToJson(c As Cell) As Json
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(n)
            JNum(n)
        Case CutStr(s)
            JStr(s)
        Case CutBool(b)
            JBool(b)
        Case CutList(xs)
            JcListToJson(xs)
        Case Else
            JStr(CutShow(c, CutFmtStd()))

Rem A LIST is an object when every element is a PAIR keyed by a STRING,
Rem and an array otherwise — the same test DcPairs applies for a dict,
Rem so a value built by DPUT reads back out through JSONTEXT unchanged.
Def JcListToJson(xs As List Of Cell) As Json
    If JcAllStrPairs(xs) Then
        JObj(Map(xs, JcMemberOf))
    Else
        JArr(Map(xs, JcToJson))

Def JcAllStrPairs(xs As List Of Cell) As Boolean
    Not IsEmpty(xs) And All(xs, JcIsStrPair)

Def JcIsStrPair(c As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case c
        Case CutPair(p)
            JcIsStr(Fst(p))
        Case Else
            False

Def JcIsStr(c As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(s)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def JcMemberOf(c As Cell) As Pair
    Select Case c
        Case CutPair(p)
            JcMemberKeyed(Fst(p), Snd(p))
        Case Else
            Pair("", JNull)

Def JcMemberKeyed(k As Cell, v As Cell) As Pair
    Select Case k
        Case CutStr(s)
            Pair(s, JcToJson(v))
        Case Else
            Pair("", JNull)

Rem Total the other way too: JNull is the one Json shape with no cell
Rem of its own, so it takes the empty list — see THE ONE GAP above.
Def JcOfJson(j As Json) As Cell
    Select Case j
        Case JNull
            CutList({ })
        Case JBool(b)
            CutBool(b)
        Case JNum(n)
            CutNum(n)
        Case JStr(s)
            CutStr(s)
        Case JArr(items)
            CutList(Map(items, JcOfJson))
        Case JObj(members)
            CutList(Map(members, JcPairOf))
        Case Else
            CutList({ })

Def JcPairOf(p As Pair) As Cell
    CutPair(Pair(CutStr(Fst(p)), JcOfJson(Snd(p))))

Rem ---- JSONPARSE ------------------------------------------------------

Def JsSeedJsonparse(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "JSONPARSE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => JsJsonparse(vs)), "( str -- doc )", "The string, parsed as JSON — objects become dicts, arrays become lists.")

Def JsJsonparse(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("JSONPARSE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            JsJsonparseRead(JsonRead(s))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONPARSE did not answer")

Def JsJsonparseRead(r As JRead) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case JOk(doc)
            RckVals({ JcOfJson(doc) })
        Case JErr(why, at)
            RckWorkBad("JSONPARSE: " & why & " AT " & Str(at))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONPARSE did not answer")

Rem ---- JSONTEXT ---------------------------------------------------------

Def JsSeedJsontext(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "JSONTEXT", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutStr(JsonText(JcToJson(First(vs)))) })), "( doc -- str )", "The value, written out as compact JSON text.")

Rem ---- JSONPRETTY ---------------------------------------------------------

Def JsSeedJsonpretty(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "JSONPRETTY", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => JsJsonpretty(vs)), "( doc n -- str )", "The value, written out as JSON text indented n spaces per level.")

Def JsJsonpretty(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("JSONPRETTY", Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(n)
            RckVals({ CutStr(JsonPretty(JcToJson(Nth(vs, 1)), n)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONPRETTY did not answer")

Rem ---- JSONLOAD -----------------------------------------------------------

Def JsSeedJsonload(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "JSONLOAD", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => JsJsonload(vs)), "( path -- doc )", "The file, read and parsed as JSON — a refusal names why it could not be, whether that is the file or the syntax.")

Def JsJsonload(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("JSONLOAD", First(vs))
        Case Ok(path)
            JsJsonloadRead(TryReadFile(path))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONLOAD did not answer")

Def JsJsonloadRead(r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(text)
            JsJsonparseRead(JsonRead(text))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("JSONLOAD: cannot read the file")
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONLOAD: cannot read the file")

Rem ---- JSONSAVE -----------------------------------------------------------
Rem True/False like WRITELINES, not a refusal: the write already
Rem happened or it did not, and the caller decides what that means
Rem rather than losing the rest of the line to it.

Def JsSeedJsonsave(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "JSONSAVE", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => JsJsonsave(vs)), "( path doc -- ok )", "Write the value to path as JSON text; True on success.")

Def JsJsonsave(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("JSONSAVE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(path)
            RckVals({ CutBool(TryWriteFile(path, JsonText(JcToJson(Nth(vs, 2))))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("JSONSAVE did not answer")

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedJson(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = JsSeedJsonparse(st)
    Let s2 = JsSeedJsontext(s1)
    Let s3 = JsSeedJsonpretty(s2)
    Let s4 = JsSeedJsonload(s3)
    JsSeedJsonsave(s4)
